# CLAUDE.md — AvyCloud

> **GOLDENE REGEL: Production darf NIEMALS negativ beeinflusst werden.**
> Kein Breaking Change. Kein Datenverlust. Kein Downtime.

## Session-Start

1. Lies diese Datei
2. Lies `TASKS.md` — aktive Tasks + Bugs
3. Bei Feature-Arbeit: lies `docs/features/<ID>/spec.md`
4. `cd backend && npm test` + `npm run build` — Baseline prüfen

## Architektur (Kurzform)

- **Frontend:** React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind → Firebase Hosting (`dist/`)
- **Backend:** Node.js 20 + Express (CommonJS) → Cloud Run (europe-west3, 3Gi/2CPU, min 1 Instance)
- **DB:** Firestore (Primary: `products_v2`, Legacy `products` = read-only)
- **KI:** Google Gemini API (`@google/genai` SDK), Vertex AI
- **Auth:** Firebase Authentication → `requireAuth()` Middleware → `req.user`
- **Integrations:** eBay, Kaufland, SendCloud, SevDesk, BrightData (Web Unlocker), SerpAPI
- **Deployment:** Push auf `main` → GitHub Actions (Frontend) + Cloud Build (Backend)

## Firestore Collections (Kernübersicht)

| Bereich | Collections |
|---------|-------------|
| **Produkte** | `products_v2` (primary), `products` (legacy, read-only), `images`, `versions` |
| **Bestellungen** | `orders`, `order_events`, `order_settings`, `shipments`, `returns`, `return_events` |
| **Warehouse** | `warehouseZones`, `warehouseBins`, `warehouse_movements`, `warehouse_settings`, `warehouseEvents` |
| **Lager/Stock** | `stock_sync_log`, `stock_sync_failures`, `stock_operation_failures`, `stock_reservations`, `stock_reconciliation_log` |
| **Marketplace** | `ebayListingsLive`, `ebayListingLinks`, `ebayListingGaps`, `kauflandUnitsLive` |
| **Pricing** | `priceHistory`, `pricingRules` |
| **System** | `company_settings`, `user_profiles`, `integrations`, `api_keys`, `webhooks`, `identificationJobs`, `gpsrManufacturers` |

Alle Collections sind tenant-scoped (tenantId-Feld oder Composite-ID wie `{tenantId}__{type}`).

## Multi-Tenancy

- Auth-Middleware (`lib/auth.js`): Bearer Token → Firebase `verifyIdToken()` → `req.user`
- TenantId-Auflösung: `req.user?.tenantId || 'default'` (Helper in jeder Route)
- **Jede** Firestore-Query braucht `.where('tenantId', '==', tenantId)`
- Config-Collections nutzen Tenant als Doc-ID: `company_settings/{tenantId}`
- Integrations nutzen Composite-IDs: `integrations/{tenantId}__{type}`

## Backend-Struktur

### Route-Prefix-Schema

Alle Routes unter `/api/`:
- `/api/auth` — Auth (public)
- `/api/webhooks/*` — Externe Webhooks (public, SendCloud etc.)
- `/api/warehouse` — Warehouse-Management
- `/api/admin` — Admin-Funktionen
- `/api/v1/rules` — Rule Engine
- `/api/sessions` — User Sessions
- `/api/*` — Orders, Products, Identify, Marketplace, Integrations, Settings, Returns, Invoices, SSE (alle authenticated)

Health-Checks: `GET /health`, `GET /ready`

### lib/ vs services/

- **`lib/`** = Low-Level: API-Clients, Utilities, Policies, Validation (z.B. `ebay-api.js`, `gemini3-client.js`, `product-store.js`, `rate-limit.js`)
- **`services/`** = Business-Logik: Runner, Engines, Event-Handler (z.B. `order-state-machine.js`, `sync-event-bus.js`, `job-runner.js`, `enrichment-v2.js`)

### Error Handling

- **AppError-Klasse** in `lib/error-handler.js`: `new AppError(code, message, statusCode)`
- **Error-Codes**: `INTERNAL`, `INTERNAL_ERROR`, `RATE_LIMITED`, `VALIDATION`, `EBAY_API_ERROR`, `KAUFLAND_API_ERROR`
- **Pattern in Routes**: try/catch mit `console.error('[METHOD /path]', err)` + JSON-Response `{ ok: false, error: { code, message } }`
- **Async-Fehler**: `lib/error-collector.js` → `collectError()` für Background-Failures

### Logging

- **Pino** (`lib/logger.js`) — Structured JSON, Cloud Run severity mapping (DEBUG/INFO/WARNING/ERROR/CRITICAL)
- **Request-Logging**: `pino-http` (`lib/request-logger.js`), ignoriert `/health` + `/ready`
- **Level**: `LOG_LEVEL` ENV-Var, Default `info`
- **In Services/Runners**: `console.*` mit Prefix `[sync-bus]`, `[order-sync]` etc.

### Rate Limiting & Queues

- **Global**: `express-rate-limit` — 120 req/min pro User
- **Identify**: 30 req/15min pro User
- **eBay**: Slot-basierter Rate Limiter (`lib/ebay-rate-limiter.js`), dynamisch via API-Headers
- **Kaufland**: Retry mit Backoff (max 4 Retries, 25s Timeout)
- **Gemini**: Retry mit Exponential Backoff (`lib/gemini-retry.js`)
- **Job Queue**: `p-queue` in `services/job-runner.js` (Concurrency 3, max 3 Attempts, 5min Timeout)
- **Event Bus**: `services/sync-event-bus.js` — In-Process EventEmitter, 5s Debounce pro Entity

### Background Runner

8 Runner in `services/`: job-runner, improve-runner, quality-runner, rulebook-runner, admin-bulk-runner, pricing-runner, listing-sync-runner, competitor-refresh-runner. Safety-Net-Intervalle in `index.js` (Order Sync 6h, Stock Reconciliation 30min, etc.).

## Frontend-Struktur

### State Management

- **React Context API** (kein Redux/Zustand): `AuthContext`, `InventoryContext`, `ToastContext`, `ProductContext`, `CookieConsentContext`
- **React Query** (`@tanstack/react-query`): Data Fetching & Cache

### API Client (`api/client.ts`)

- Fetch-basierter Wrapper mit automatischem Firebase Auth Token (`buildHeadersWithAuth()`)
- Token-Injection via `setAuthTokenProvider()` aus AuthContext
- Backend-URL: `VITE_BACKEND_URL`, Fallback-URLs für eBay-Endpoints
- Pattern für neue API-Calls: Funktion in `client.ts` exportieren, in Component/Hook konsumieren

### Routing

- **Custom Hash-based Router** in `App.tsx` (kein React Router)
- Format: `#/dashboard`, `#/sheet/{productId}`, `#/orders/returns`
- `parseHash()` → `{ view, productId }`, `setView()` für Navigation
- 37 Views total

### i18n (`i18n.tsx`)

- **3 Sprachen**: `de` (Default), `en`, `tr`
- **Pflicht**: Jeder neue UI-String muss in alle 3 Sprachen übersetzt werden
- Hook: `useI18n()` → `t('key', { vars })`
- Keys: Namespaced (`nav.*`, `auth.*`, `orders.*`, `sheet.*`)

### UI-Komponenten

- **Shared Library**: `components/ui/` (24 Komponenten) — Import via `import { Button, Modal } from '../components/ui'`
- **Feature-Ordner**: `components/settings/`, `components/orders/`, `components/chat/` etc.
- **Hooks**: 22 Custom Hooks in `hooks/` (z.B. `useProductStream`, `useSSE`, `useBarcodeScanner`, `useIdentification`)

### Types

- Zentral in `types.ts` (693 Zeilen): `Product`, `Order`, `InventoryRecord`, `WarehouseBin`, `IdentificationJob`, `DashboardMetrics` etc.

## Nicht verhandelbar

1. Keine bestehende Route ändern ohne explizite Anweisung
2. Keine Firestore-Felder umbenennen/löschen (additive only)
3. Keine Dependencies entfernen
4. Keine ENV-Vars umbenennen die in CI/CD referenziert werden
5. Keine Änderung an Dockerfile, firebase.json, cloudbuild.yaml ohne Anweisung
6. Keine Änderung an Auth (lib/auth.js, lib/rbac.js) ohne Anweisung
7. Alle Produkt-Schreibpfade über `saveProductV2()` (lib/product-store.js)
8. Alle neuen Queries/Collections mit `tenantId`
9. **BaseLinker ist TABU** — keine neuen Referenzen, Imports oder ENV-Vars
10. Alle neuen UI-Strings in alle 3 Sprachen (de/en/tr) in `i18n.tsx`
11. Neue UI-Farben nur über Design-Tokens — niemals raw Tailwind Colors

## Code-Stil

- **Backend:** CommonJS (`require`/`module.exports`), 2 Spaces, Single Quotes, async/await, try/catch mit AppError
- **Frontend:** TypeScript ESM, 2 Spaces, Double Quotes, Functional Components + Hooks
- **UI-Farben:** Nur Design-Tokens (`bg-accent`, `text-txt-primary`, nicht `bg-blue-500`). Siehe `styles/main.css`
- **Status-Farben:** `success`/`warning`/`danger`/`info` + `-dim` Varianten
- **Tests:** Vitest, `cd backend && npm test`. Jede neue Funktion braucht min. 1 Test. CJS-Tests nutzen `require.cache`-Patching (kein `vi.mock`)
- **Git:** Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`), kein Force-Push auf main

## Deployment

- **Frontend**: Push auf `main` → GitHub Actions → `npm run build` → Firebase Hosting (Site: `avycloud`)
- **Backend**: Cloud Build → Docker Build → Cloud Run Deploy (Service: `product-hub-backend`)
- **Cloud Run Config**: 3Gi RAM, 2 CPU, min 1 Instance, Timeout 600s, `USE_PRODUCTS_V2=true`
- **Firestore Indexes**: `firestore.indexes.json` (12 Composite Indexes, tenantId + createdAt/status Pattern)
- **Manuelles Deploy**: Push auf `main` triggert beide Pipelines automatisch

## Weiterführende Regeln

Path-scoped Rules in `.claude/rules/` werden automatisch geladen wenn relevante Dateien bearbeitet werden:
- `backend.md` — Backend Code-Stil, CJS Patterns, Test-Setup
- `frontend.md` — Token-System, Dark Mode, Markenname
- `production-safety.md` — Red/Yellow Zone Dateien
- `workflow.md` — Agent-Workflow, Wann stoppen
- `decisions.md` — Architektur-Entscheidungen (products_v2, BaseLinker, OMS, Design)

Feature-Specs unter `docs/features/<ID>/spec.md` enthalten alle Details pro Feature.
